              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Kannada for to pay, then the Kannada for to bathe."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: ಸುಲಿ",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ಸುಲಿ — suli — \"to peel\"."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ಸುಲಿ (suli) is native Dravidian, one word with Tamil coli- (DEDR 2856). DEDR lists suli itself, \"to strip off, peel\". Its note compares an Indo-Aryan verb, Prakrit chollaï, \"to skin\" (CDIAL 5073), and leaves the direction of borrowing open."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for this chapter."
            }
          ]
        },
